While the sensor is exposed to a reducing gas (such as methanol gas), the methanol gas molecules react with the absorbed oxygen on the material surface, and this will lead to electrons being released back to the semiconductor from adsorbed oxygen species, resulting in a decrease in the conductivity. The reaction between methanol gas molecules and adsorbed oxygen can be described as (9):9\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
