In addition to the formation of a p-n heterojunction, the large specific surface and the high amount of adsorbed oxygen also attributed to improving the sensing performance. The order of specific surface area was S3 > S2 > S1 > S4, and the sensing responses of the four sensors were in the same order. This indicates that a large specific surface area is beneficial for sensing response, which provides more active sites for both the target gas and oxygen molecules and favors the surface catalytic reaction. S3 exhibits a higher ratio of \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
